===Verb===
{{en-verb|potashes|potashing|potashed}}

# To [[treat]] with [[potassium]].
#* {{quote-book|year=1910|title=Platers' Guide: With which is Combined Brass World |author= |page= |ISBN= |passage=In order to ascertain the difference between the rapidity of pickling when the tin frames had been '''potashed''' and pickling without such treatment, two batches were used.  }}
#* {{quote-book|year=1915 |title=Metal Finishing: Preparation, Electroplating, Coating |author= |page= |ISBN= |passage=Gold ornaments are sand blasted or steel brushed nicely, then '''potashed''', }}
#* {{quote-book|year=1953|title=Nature Magazine  |author= |page=223 |ISBN= |passage=After removal from a worker bee they should be '''potashed''' in ten percent potassium hydroxide, washed, dehydrated, cleared, and mounted. }}
#* {{quote-book|year=2003|title=Senckenbergiana biologica  |author= |page=136 |ISBN= |passage=For the extraction of the internal sclerites the aedeagus was '''potashed''' in cold saturated KOH solution for several hours and transferred to a vial of distilled water.  }}

